00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:16.270
Yeah!

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:28.920
He's up
there.

00:17:29.090 --> 00:17:29.920
Let's move it!

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:30.820
Okay!

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:35.660
So much for that!

00:17:36.300 --> 00:17:39.790
No need for your monster
strength here.

00:17:39.970 --> 00:17:41.560
Just a minute
there...

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:44.000
Must be my
turn.

00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:47.560
Seeing as I'm
the lightest.

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:56.850
Akimoto, are you okay?

00:17:56.850 --> 00:18:01.080
Huh?! What're you doing here?!

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:03.520
Keep your voice down!

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:05.990
I said, what are you doing here?!

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:09.460
I'm here to save you,
what do you think?!

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:13.000
I don't want to be
saved by you!

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:15.340
Huh?

00:18:18.510 --> 00:18:20.870
You peed your pants!

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:22.740
Leave me alone!

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:24.780
Oh, no!

00:18:32.020 --> 00:18:32.820
Natsumi!

00:18:32.990 --> 00:18:33.610
Okay!

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:44.760
Thank goodness!

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:48.260
Looks like we saved
both of them!

00:18:48.570 --> 00:18:50.160
Are they all
right?

00:18:50.340 --> 00:18:51.930
Yasuyo!

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:54.270
Huh?

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:58.740
What?! Who's running
the crane?!

00:18:59.710 --> 00:19:01.620
Hang on tight.

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:03.480
We'll be okay, if we can keep quiet.

00:19:03.650 --> 00:19:04.550
Huh?

00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:05.740
What was that?

00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:08.220
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:11.560
Me, too!

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:12.960
I knew it!

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:15.090
Oh, no! Not
now!

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:20.360
Just hang on! I'm the adored
leader of the Strike Brigade!

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:21.960
Well, if it isn't my
archrival...

00:19:22.070 --> 00:19:23.870
...Home Run Girl!

00:19:24.440 --> 00:19:25.840
Nerd!

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:30.380
Strike Man, Defender of Justice,
is coming to rescue you!

00:19:39.520 --> 00:19:40.920
Yasuyo!

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:50.960
We're gonna die!

00:19:51.100 --> 00:19:52.530
This is awful!

00:19:52.970 --> 00:19:55.830
We have to be quiet if we're
gonna get out of here!

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:57.900
Huh?! What'd
you say?

00:20:00.370 --> 00:20:01.740
Keep it down!

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:05.900
What's that?
Speak up!

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:09.520
I'm telling you to keep
your fat mouth shut!

00:20:12.790 --> 00:20:15.720
I get it!

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:27.570
I mustn't
miss!

00:20:31.340 --> 00:20:32.200
Natsumi!

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:33.030
Gotcha!

00:20:48.360 --> 00:20:50.190
We made it!

00:20:50.360 --> 00:20:51.450
Somehow!

00:20:53.090 --> 00:20:55.390
You guys are unreal!

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:58.300
Hey, thanks!

00:21:00.970 --> 00:21:03.300
It was nothing.

00:21:08.680 --> 00:21:10.340
Uh... I'm sorry.

00:21:10.810 --> 00:21:12.640
Me, too.

00:21:13.110 --> 00:21:16.810
Don't tell anybody about this
Strike Brigade thing.

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:18.220
Otherwise... I'll tell everyone...

00:21:18.220 --> 00:21:20.020
Yeah, I understand!

00:21:20.190 --> 00:21:23.020
Well, I guess we've wrapped
up this one.

00:21:23.190 --> 00:21:23.690
Yeah.

00:21:23.690 --> 00:21:24.490
Not quite!

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:25.390
Huh?

00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:29.460
Have you forgotten our destiny; you
and I challenging each other?!

00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:31.560
Come on everyone, time
to go home now.

00:21:31.730 --> 00:21:33.460
Don't even listen
to him.

00:21:33.630 --> 00:21:35.120
Yes, Ma'am!

00:21:35.300 --> 00:21:37.240
Take heed, Home
Run Girl!

00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:45.440
Savor my latest sure-death weapon,
the Great Spiral Thunderball!

00:21:45.680 --> 00:21:47.700
Hey! Are you listening
to me, or what?!

00:21:47.810 --> 00:21:51.440
Hey! Home
Run Girl?!

00:22:05.700 --> 00:22:07.700
<i>I live my life my own way, doing</i>
<i>things others wouldn't.</i>

00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:19.880
<i>Being strong isn't enough.</i>
<i>It makes me Ionely.</i>

00:22:22.580 --> 00:22:30.890
<i>I can feel your presence</i>
<i>as if you're right here...</i>

00:22:31.430 --> 00:22:38.990
<i>... but I can't say a word.</i>

00:22:40.530 --> 00:22:47.800
<i>The feelings I hide within might</i>
<i>break into pieces...</i>

00:22:49.340 --> 00:22:56.650
<i>But if I don't say anything,</i>
<i>nothing can begin.</i>

00:22:56.980 --> 00:23:04.210
<i>The wind gently blows...</i>
<i>Time flows...</i>

00:23:04.390 --> 00:23:13.930
<i>Time flows... And soon</i>
<i>I can be honest...</i>

00:23:14.070 --> 00:23:17.030
<i>Thank you,</i>
<i>friend!</i>

00:23:23.240 --> 00:23:25.070
"Legend of a Dreamchaser"

00:23:26.280 --> 00:23:28.980
Daimaru and Sena have opened
their bike shop...

00:23:29.080 --> 00:23:32.050
...so Nakajima and I go over
to help them celebrate.

00:23:32.750 --> 00:23:37.880
Meanwhile, Natsumi meets
an old man in a garage.

00:23:38.230 --> 00:23:42.390
The man turns out to be a legendary
motorcycle mechanic.

00:23:43.630 --> 00:23:47.670
Next time on You're Under Arrest, File 19,
"The Broken Dream of a Bike Mechanic."

00:23:47.800 --> 00:23:49.800
Hey! Let's do it!
